TY  - GEN
TI  - Extensive Hydroxyl Groups (Mucilage): Create viscous gel through hydrogen bonding with water; physical protective barrier
ER  - 

TY  - GEN
TI  - Cyclopentane-Pyran System (Iridoids): Rigid structure for specific receptor binding; antimicrobial and anti-inflammatory activities
ER  - 

TY  - GEN
TI  - Catechol Groups (Verbascoside): Powerful electron donors for antioxidant activity; enzyme inhibition
ER  - 

TY  - GEN
TI  - Amphipathic Saponins: Enable membrane disruption for antimicrobial effects; reduce surface tension for expectorant action
ER  - 

TY  - GEN
TI  - Glycosylation: Enhances water solubility and bioavailability; modulates biological activity
ER  - 

TY  - GEN
TI  - Ester Linkages (Verbascoside): Provides metabolic lability; releases active components after hydrolysis
