TY  - GEN
TI  - Quaternary Nitrogen in Alkaloids (Magnoflorine, Berberine): [512] Permanent positive charge enhances membrane interactions Increases affinity for anionic binding sites Facilitates DNA intercalation (planar structure + positive charge)
ER  - 

TY  - GEN
TI  - Multiple Hydroxyl Groups (Flavonoids): [213] Hydrogen bond donors for protein interactions Electron donors for free radical scavenging Sites for Phase II metabolism (glucuronidation, sulfation)
ER  - 

TY  - GEN
TI  - Planar Aromatic Systems: [12] π-π stacking with biological targets DNA intercalation capability Resonance stabilization of radical intermediates
ER  - 

TY  - GEN
TI  - Catechol Groups (ortho-dihydroxy structure): [13] Strong metal chelation (Fe³⁺, Cu²⁺) Enhanced antioxidant activity COX/LOX enzyme inhibition
ER  - 

TY  - GEN
TI  - Lipophilicity: [21] Cell membrane permeability Ability to reach intracellular targets Accumulation in lipid-rich tissues
ER  - 

TY  - GEN
TI  - Amphipathic Character (Saponins): [ 4 ] Interaction with both aqueous and lipid environments Membrane disruption capabilities Surfactant properties
ER  - 

TY  - GEN
TI  - Proper Identification: Ensure correct species; some toxic look-alikes exist
