TY  - GEN
TI  - Multiple Hydroxyl Groups: The phenolic -OH groups act as hydrogen donors for antioxidant activity and form hydrogen bonds with biological targets.
ER  - 

TY  - GEN
TI  - Planar Aromatic Systems: Allow π-π stacking interactions with proteins and DNA, and provide resonance stabilization of radical intermediates.
ER  - 

TY  - GEN
TI  - Amphipathic Nature (Saponins): Enables interaction with both lipid membranes and aqueous environments, crucial for antimicrobial activity.
ER  - 

TY  - GEN
TI  - Chelation Sites: Catechol groups and keto-enol systems chelate metal ions, preventing oxidative damage.
ER  - 

TY  - GEN
TI  - Lipophilicity: Allows compounds to cross cell membranes and reach intracellular targets.
